<title>USA: McDonald's expands into Peru.</title>
<headline>McDonald's expands into Peru.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill.</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald's Corp. said Thursday it will open its first restaurant in Lima, Peru, on Friday, making Peru the 96th country in which the fast-food giant does business and the 24th country in the Latin America/Caribbean region.</p>
<p>McDonald's said it expects to do business in 100 countries by year-end.</p>
<p>In the last five years, the number of McDonald's restaurants in Latin America and the Caribbean has more than tripled, with the company now operating nearly 650 outlets there. Worldwide, McDonald's has more than 19,200 fast food restaurants.</p>
